{"id":3736,"path":"/grammar-points/a1/possessive-adjectives/","parentId":540,"order":20,"section":"grammar-points","level":"a1","depth":3,"title":"Possessive adjectives and subject pronouns (I/my, you/your, etc.)","seo":{"title":"Possessive adjectives and subject pronouns (I/my, you/your, etc.) - Test-English","description":"Learn how to use possessive adjectives in this A1 Elementary grammar lesson. Clear rules, charts and exercises. Practise now!","image":"/media/uploads/A1%E2%80%93Grammar_Possessive-Adjectives.png"},"modified":"2026-02-18T09:07:36","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose the correct subject pronouns or possessive adjectives to complete the sentences.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"421\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Choose the correct subject pronouns or possessive adjectives to complete the following sentences.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"422\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Fill in the gaps with the correct possessive adjectives: <em>my, your, his, her, its, our, their</em>.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"423\"></div>"],"explanation":"<h2>Possessive adjectives and subject pronouns</h2> <h3>Form</h3> <p><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-10806\" src=\"/media/uploads/possessive-adjectives-new.png\" alt=\"Grammar chart showing the relationship between subject pronouns and possessive adjectives in English with examples such as 'I/my', 'you/your', and 'he/his'.\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h3>Use</h3> <h4><strong>I</strong> + verb / <strong>My</strong> + noun</h4> <p>We use&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/object-pronouns/\">subject pronoun</a></strong> <strong>+ verb</strong>, and we use <strong>possessive adjective + noun</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>These are Susan and Thomas; <span><strong>they</strong></span> are from Ohio. And that’s <span><strong>their</strong></span> house.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em><span><strong>I</strong></span> love <span><strong>my</strong></span> friend Sheila.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <h4>Possessive adjectives are always singular</h4> <p><a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/adjectives/\">Adjectives</a> in English have no plural form.&nbsp;Possessive adjectives are always singular.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>These are <span><strong>their</strong></span> suitcases. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>These are <span><strong>theirs</strong></span> suitcases. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> </ul> <h4><strong>It/its</strong> for things, <strong>they/their</strong>&nbsp;for people and things</h4> <p>We use <strong>he/his</strong> and <strong>she/her</strong> for people, and we use&nbsp;<strong>it/its</strong> for things. But in the plural, we use&nbsp;<strong>they/their</strong> for people and things.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><i>The hotel has <span><strong>its</strong></span> own spa. <span><strong>It</strong></span> is a relaxing place.&nbsp;</i></li> <li><em>I like those chairs, <span><strong>they</strong></span> are beautiful. But <span><strong>their</strong></span> legs are too long.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <h4><strong>It’s</strong> for time and weather</h4> <p>We use&nbsp;<strong>it’s (=it is)&nbsp;</strong>to talk about the time or the weather.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em><span><strong>It’s</strong> </span>very windy today, but <span><strong>it’s</strong></span> sunny.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>‘What time <span><strong>is it</strong></span>?’ ‘<span><strong>It’s</strong></span> three o’clock.’</em></li> </ul> <h4><strong>Its</strong> or <strong>it’s</strong>?</h4> <p><strong>Its</strong> = possessive adjective. <strong>It’s</strong> = <strong>it is</strong> (subject + verb&nbsp;<strong>be</strong>)</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>Look at that dog. <span><strong>It’s</strong></span> beautiful. I like <span><strong>its</strong></span> hair.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul>","quizzes":[{"id":421,"questions":[{"id":3636,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Harry is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> friend. <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> has a nice house. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["my","I"]},{"kind":"select","options":["His","He"]}]},{"id":3637,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span> are very happy with <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> new dog. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["They","Their"]},{"kind":"select","options":["they","their"]}]},{"id":3638,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We love <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> little dog. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["we","our"]}]},{"id":3639,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span> wants <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> breakfast. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["He","His"]},{"kind":"select","options":["he","his"]}]},{"id":3640,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We want to see <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> children. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["our","ours"]}]},{"id":3641,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Scotland is famous for <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> rainy weather. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["its","it's"]}]},{"id":3642,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Susan lives on <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> street. <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> house is very near. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["my","I"]},{"kind":"select","options":["His","Her"]}]},{"id":3643,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>'What are those?' '<span data-gap=\"0\"></span> postcards.'</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["They are","It is"]}]},{"id":3644,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I like this place and <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> special atmosphere. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["its","it's"]}]},{"id":3645,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I love this place. <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> very special. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["Its","It's"]}]}]},{"id":422,"questions":[{"id":3646,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Go to _____ office. </div>","choices":[{"id":5763,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>you</span>"},{"id":5764,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>your</span>"},{"id":5765,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>yours</span>"}]},{"id":3657,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>_____ six o'clock. Let's go home. </div>","choices":[{"id":5766,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>It's</span>"},{"id":5767,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>Its</span>"},{"id":5768,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>His</span>"}]},{"id":3658,"num":"3","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Our products are famous for _____ durability.</div>","choices":[{"id":5769,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>their</span>"},{"id":5770,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>its</span>"},{"id":5771,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>they</span>"}]},{"id":3659,"num":"4","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I'm very happy about _____ marks.</div>","choices":[{"id":5772,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>you</span>"},{"id":5773,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>your</span>"},{"id":5774,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>yours</span>"}]},{"id":3660,"num":"5","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Valeria is from Italy, but _____ 's in Ireland now. </div>","choices":[{"id":5775,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>his</span>"},{"id":5776,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>her</span>"},{"id":5777,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>she</span>"}]},{"id":3661,"num":"6","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>These are my friends. _____ from Finland. </div>","choices":[{"id":5778,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>Their</span>"},{"id":5779,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>They're</span>"},{"id":5780,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>They</span>"}]},{"id":3662,"num":"7","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>The apartment has _____ own private garden. </div>","choices":[{"id":5781,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>it's</span>"},{"id":5782,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>its</span>"},{"id":5783,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>his</span>"}]},{"id":3663,"num":"8","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Are _____ umbrellas here?</div>","choices":[{"id":5784,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>we</span>"},{"id":5785,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>ours</span>"},{"id":5786,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>our</span>"}]},{"id":3664,"num":"9","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Mark and Linda are in _____ caravan. </div>","choices":[{"id":5787,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>they</span>"},{"id":5788,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>their</span>"},{"id":5789,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>its</span>"}]},{"id":3665,"num":"10","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I need _____ tools, please. </div>","choices":[{"id":5790,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>your</span>"},{"id":5791,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>you</span>"},{"id":5792,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>yours</span>"}]}]},{"id":423,"questions":[{"id":3647,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Sally is in <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> room.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3648,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Paul and Benet always help <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> friends.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3649,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We live with <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> parents.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3650,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Is that <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> hat?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3651,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The police officers don't have <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> guns.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3655,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The best part of this car is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> price.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3652,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Amanda lives with <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> parents.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3653,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I don't like <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> new job.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3654,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>These shoes are famous for <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> comfort.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3656,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Thomas is in <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> office.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]}]}]}